# Codex Adversarial Review

Target: branch diff against main
Verdict: needs-attention

Dense phone cells can clip the new unanswered count. Fix the layout before shipping.

Findings:
- [medium] Wrapped dense counts exceed the square phone cell (src/features/group/calendar/DayCell.tsx:121-123)
  At 390px, the calendar leaves about 30px of content width per cell. A supported 100-player day with 30 free, 30 busy and 40 unanswered requires three count lines. Those lines plus the date exceed the fixed aspect-square cell height, whose overflow-hidden clips the lower counts. This follows from the layout dimensions; browser confirmation was blocked by the read-only sandbox. The existing 12-player screenshot case does not cover this limit.
  Recommendation: Give dense cells enough minimum height for the date and three count lines, or use a count layout that fits the available space. Verify that all counts remain visible at 390px with two-digit free, busy and unanswered counts.

Next steps:
- Check the corrected dense layout at 390px with 30 free, 30 busy and 40 unanswered players.
